{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_116067546", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "A quantum computer could pose a significant threat to Bitcoin through a 51% attack by leveraging its superior computational power, potentially enabling it to control more than half of the network's hashrate.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1081726807#13_2144947963", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1081726807#12_2144946346"]}, {"text": "Experts are concerned about the potential threat from quantum computers to blockchain technology, including Bitcoin, due to their ability to perform complex calculations much faster than classical computers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1396617945#13_1573528319"]}, {"text": "The National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) is developing post-quantum cryptography algorithms, which could be available as early as 2022 to protect against quantum computing threats.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1081726807#17_2144955415"]}, {"text": "The computational power of current classical computers is significantly lower than that of potential quantum computers, making a 51% attack by quantum computers more feasible in the future.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2337990636#8_2586311044"]}, {"text": "A double spend attack by a quantum computer could be more efficient than classical computers due to the speed at which they can process complex transactions, potentially disrupting transaction confirmations.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1396617945#13_1573528319"]}, {"text": "Post-quantum cryptography aims to protect blockchain technology from quantum computing threats by developing algorithms that are resistant to attacks from both classical and quantum computers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2337990636#8_2586311044"]}, {"text": "As of 2023, the cryptocurrency community is aware of the potential threat from quantum computing and is taking steps to prepare for it with researching post-quantum cryptography solutions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1396617945#13_1573528319"]}, {"text": "Experts predict that quantum computers will be powerful enough to pose a significant threat to Bitcoin's security in the coming years, as advancements in technology continue to increase their computational capabilities.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_1396617945#13_1573528319"]}, {"text": "The cryptocurrency community is taking various steps to prepare for potential quantum computing threats, including developing and implementing post-quantum cryptography algorithms.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1081726807#13_2144947963"]}]}
