g Bang, two universes were formed: ours and one running in reverse with time going backward. This was mentioned in a segment citing 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_493214644#4_969694431'.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_493214644#4_969694431"]}, {"text": "Other reputable news outlets, such as The New York Post and others, have reported on the ANITA experiment findings, suggesting that time could run backwards in a parallel universe. A segment citing 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#7_1610053245' supports this claim.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#7_1610053245"]}, {"text": "The New York Post reported that the simplest explanation for the phenomenon observed by Peter Gorham and his team is that at the moment of the Big Bang, two universes were formed: ours and one running in reverse with time going backward. This was mentioned in a segment citing 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#7_1610053245'.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_819561425#7_1610053245"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_515287844", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The French media commentator's claim about churches being desecrated in France in 2019 is supported by independent sources. In February 2019, there were at least 10 incidents of vandalism and desecration of churches and Christian monuments in France.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1187732256#16_2752800655"]}, {"text": "French National Assembly member Val\u00e9rie Boyer (LR) and others tabled a motion for a resolution calling for the creation of a committee of inquiry into the policy of preventing and combating desecration of places of worship and cemeteries in France, following the incidents reported in 2019.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1187732256#16_2752800655"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_730773621", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Belle Delphine created a Pornhub account in June 2019 after reaching 1 million likes on a post.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2250946488#10_2490788386"]}, {"text": "She launched an online store selling 'GamerGirl Bath Water' on July 1, 2019.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_260495005#9_593655593"]}, {"text": "Rumors circulated about people contracting herpes from the bathwater, but no evidence exists.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_260495005#9_593655593"]}, {"text": "A controversial video showed her dancing to a suicide song in February 2019.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2250946488#6_2490781555"]}, {"text": "False rumors of Belle Delphine's death spread online in 2019 without credible evidence.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2250946488#6_2490781555"]}, {"text": "Between October 2018 and July 2019, she was involved with three companies: Innovative Artists, Plain Jane Investments, and Belle Store.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2250946488#10_2490788386"]}, {"text": "Indigo White alleged that underage Delphine passed off other people's photos as her own.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2250946488#6_2490781555"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1289995263", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Graham Ivan Clark was a 17-year-old when he was arrested for the Twitter hack.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_788653296#2_1631962963", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#6_1840416800"]}, {"text": "Graham Ivan Clark was a 17-year-old when he was arrested for the Twitter hack.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_788653296#2_1631962963", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#6_1840416800"]}, {"text": "Initially, 130 Twitter accounts were believed to be compromised during the hack, and hackers tweeted messages from 45 of them to lure victims into sending Bitcoin.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#7_1840418677", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1317702012#3_1505585222"]}, {"text": "Initially, 130 Twitter accounts were believed to be compromised during the hack, and hackers tweeted messages from 45 of them to lure victims into sending Bitcoin.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#7_1840418677", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1317702012#3_1505585222"]}, {"text": "The specific charges filed against Graham Ivan Clark include 30 felony charges for scamming people across America and perpetrating the 'Bit-Con' hack of prominent Twitter accounts.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#7_1840418677"]}, {"text": "The legal system will handle the case by prosecuting Graham Ivan Clark in his hometown of Tampa, Florida.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#6_1840416800"]}, {"text": "Graham Ivan Clark managed to collect more than $10,000 in Bitcoin through the scam during the Twitter hack.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#7_1840418677"]}, {"text": "Twitter responded to the hack by acknowledging it as embarrassing, but there is no mention of specific security measures they implemented after the incident in the given segments.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_856282060#7_1840418677"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1666095905", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Other major news outlets, such as those cited in 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724' and 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#3_3112397911', have reported on the proposed European Super League, with statements from club owners, players, or fans opposing the plan.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#3_3112397911"]}, {"text": "Other major news outlets, such as those cited in 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724' and 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#3_3112397911', have reported on the proposed European Super League, with statements from club owners, players, or fans opposing the plan.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#3_3112397911"]}, {"text": "According to 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724', the estimated earning for each club signing up to the proposed Super League is $600 million per year, a figure that has not been confirmed by other sources.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724"]}, {"text": "The Premier League, as reported in 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724', has stated that the proposed European Super League would have a detrimental impact on domestic competitions and player development.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724"]}, {"text": "FIFA and UEFA, as cited in 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724', have condemned the proposed European Super League, stating that it would undermine the integrity of international football competitions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724"]}, {"text": "Politicians and governments, as reported in 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724', have expressed concern over the proposed European Super League, with some considering legislative actions to prevent its formation.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724"]}, {"text": "The format and structure of the proposed European Super League, as described in 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776', would include 20 teams with a mix of existing top clubs and new entrants, differing from the Champions League format.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_607661422#6_656736776"]}, {"text": "The collapse of the proposed European Super League, as reported in 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724', was largely due to opposition from club owners and players, with some clubs like Bayern Munich rejecting the plan.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1342059431#4_3112399724"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_304836636", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Sweden aims for full cashlessness by March 2023.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_896216492#4_1841576376"]}, {"text": "Security concerns include device dependency and loss of physical currency.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_1528108616#0_3225939925"]}, {"text": "Small businesses see benefits but face operational challenges.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_1107869806#6_2425945768"]}, {"text": "Sweden's digital payment adoption is more advanced than other developed nations.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_896216492#0_1841569233"]}, {"text": "Consumer fears involve device dependency and financial insecurity.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_1528108616#0_3225939925"]}, {"text": "Credit scores may rely on transaction data in a cashless society.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_1107869806#6_2425945768"]}, {"text": "Pros include reduced costs and convenience; cons are security risks and business challenges.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_130476167#6_249854865"]}, {"text": "Operational issues like payment service interoperability could hinder the transition.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_130476167#6_249854865"]}, {"text": "Traditional businesses might struggle with cashless systems.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_1107869806#6_2425945768"]}, {"text": "Sweden's digital infrastructure is more advanced for full cashlessness.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_896216492#0_1841569233"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_1547893878", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' movement considers the term 'Birds Arent Real' without an apostrophe as inadvisable and always recommends using 'Birds Aren't Real'. This is supported by segment ID: 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1736074117#17_3504608097'", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1736074117#17_3504608097"]}, {"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' movement was initially aimed at preventing the extinction of real birds, but it has since shifted to making people aware that they were replaced by surveillance drones. This is supported by segment ID: 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248380023#1_563092994'", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248380023#1_563092994"]}, {"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' movement has a substantial online presence with active accounts on Instagram, Twitter, and YouTube. This is supported by segment ID: 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248380023#1_563092994'", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248380023#1_563092994"]}, {"text": "The term 'Bird Truthers' is used within the 'Birds Aren't Real' movement to refer to its supporters. This can be seen in segment ID: 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248380023#1_563092994'", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248380023#1_563092994"]}, {"text": "The 'Birds Aren't Real' movement has significant online presence with active accounts on Instagram, Twitter, and YouTube, indicating a substantial following. This is supported by segment ID: 'msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248380023#1_563092994'", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248380023#1_563092994"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_248024230", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The complaint against Apple cites specific legal sections to support the claims, including references to antitrust laws and consumer protection statutes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_1185793181#3_2591683877"]}, {"text": "Apple is accused of engaging in anti-competitive conduct by requiring software developers to use the App Store for distribution on iOS devices, thereby imposing a 30% fee.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_766155921#11_1633827852"]}, {"text": "The complaint alleges that Apple's practices harm both software developers and consumers by limiting their options for distribution and payment, respectively.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_81705500#9_204514368"]}, {"text": "The complaint references the Sherman Act as a key legal section supporting the claims against Apple for antitrust violations.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_1185793181#3_2591683877"]}, {"text": "Apple is accused of imposing a 30% fee on all software sold through the App Store, which restricts competition and harms developers by limiting their revenue potential.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_766155921#11_1633827852"]}, {"text": "The complaint argues that Apple's conduct has a pervasive anti-competitive effect, harming consumers by restricting their access to software and services.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_81705500#9_204514368"]}, {"text": "The complaint also cites the California Cartwright Act as a legal section supporting the claims against Apple for antitrust violations.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_1185793181#3_2591683877"]}, {"text": "Apple's requirement that all software on iOS devices be distributed through the App Store is seen as anti-competitive, as it limits developers' ability to reach users directly.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_766155921#11_1633827852"]}, {"text": "The complaint states that Apple's practices harm consumers by preventing them from installing software directly, which is allowed on other platforms like PC and Mac.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_81705500#9_204514368"]}, {"text": "Apple's imposition of a 30% fee on all software sold through the App Store is cited as an example of its anti-competitive conduct that restricts competition and harms developers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_766155921#11_1633827852"]}]}
