{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_1-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_58_748655897", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The idea for the Storm Area 51 events was devised by a person named Alex Carnevale, who is also known as 'Alex from YouTube'. He created the event to celebrate his birthday and promote UFO conspiracy theories.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_182434062#16_406288169"]}, {"text": "By August 22, an estimated 500,000 people had signed up for the event as 'going' or 'interested', indicating a significant level of public interest.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2430780951#5_2743916519"]}, {"text": "Air Force spokeswoman Grace Manock stated that government officials were briefed on the event and discouraged people from attempting to enter military property.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2430755795#3_2743890942", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_844455676#2_1028228264"]}, {"text": "Air Force spokeswoman Grace Manock stated that government officials were briefed on the event and discouraged people from attempting to enter military property.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2430755795#3_2743890942", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_844455676#2_1028228264"]}, {"text": "The event had an effect on businesses both locally in Nevada and around the United States, which prepared products for visitors and those attending the event.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2430780951#1_2743909583"]}, {"text": "Nevada law enforcement warned potential participants in the event against trespassing, emphasizing the importance of respecting military property.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_844455676#3_1028230097"]}, {"text": "Two music festivals were planned to coincide with the event: Alienstock in Rachel, Nevada, and Storm Area 51 Basecamp in Hiko, Nevada. An estimated 1,500 people attended these festivals according to state and local law enforcement.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2430780951#1_2743909583"]}, {"text": "The event saw significant engagement on social media platforms, particularly on Facebook and Twitter, where the Storm Area 51 meme spread widely.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2430780951#2_2743911305"]}, {"text": "Air Force spokeswoman Laura McAndrews stated in her statement to The Washington Post that government officials were briefed on the event and discouraged people from attempting to enter military property.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_844455676#3_1028230097"]}, {"text": "The historical background of Area 51 dates back to 1955 when it was established as an aircraft testing and development facility. It has since become a subject of UFO conspiracy theories due to its secretive nature and the reports of unusual activity around the site.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2430780951#2_2743911305"]}, {"text": "Other events created as copies or parodies of the Storm Area 51 event included a similar event called 'Storm Area 51 Basecamp' in Hiko, Nevada. These events were meant to mock and capitalize on the original event's popularity.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_2430780951#1_2743909583"]}]}
